(6439744, 955919, 129267, '<td valign="top">one of the few close up bee photos where composition seems deliberate. colors are wonderful, I like the breathing room up top, and the contrast of the bee. my only negative is that I''d like the image to be a hair sharper.</td>', 'one of the few close up bee photos where composition seems deliberate. colors are wonderful, I like the breathing room up top, and the contrast of the bee. my only negative is that I''d like the image to be a hair sharper.', '2011-06-09 19:31:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6439745, 955904, 129267, '<td valign="top">good focus, exposure and lighting. I think I''d like to see this a bit more simplified somehow. I get a pretty good case of vertigo from this angle.</td>', 'good focus, exposure and lighting. I think I''d like to see this a bit more simplified somehow. I get a pretty good case of vertigo from this angle.', '2011-06-09 19:33:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6439753, 955953, 129267, '<td valign="top">Not a big fan of the title, feels a bit immature, which makes it a bit harder to take the shot seriously. (just my opinion, others will have theirs.)<br/> <br/>I like the sultry use of honey, and the capture of motion. Lighting seems nice as is, but I''d be curious to see how this would look even more high-key. <br/> <br/>some of the things I find distracting in this are the water/honey drops on the leftmost side of the breast - they remind me of sweat, which takes away the allure of the shot. In addition to that, the sharp angle of flesh under the breast (is she leaning over?) would look better (imo) if it were vertical. that little flesh bit makes me feel like the model doesn''t really want the honey on her -- it just sort of removes me from the scene. <br/> <br/>honestly, I''m being nit-picky. If the trolls don''t get you, you''ll do well.</td>', 'Not a big fan of the title, feels a bit immature, which makes it a bit harder to take the shot seriously. (just my opinion, others will have theirs.) I like the sultry use of honey, and the capture of motion. Lighting seems nice as is, but I''d be curious to see how this would look even more high-key.  some of the things I find distracting in this are the water/honey drops on the leftmost side of the breast - they remind me of sweat, which takes away the allure of the shot. In addition to that, the sharp angle of flesh under the breast (is she leaning over?) would look better (imo) if it were vertical. that little flesh bit makes me feel like the model doesn''t really want the honey on her -- it just sort of removes me from the scene.  honestly, I''m being nit-picky. If the trolls don''t get you, you''ll do well.', '2011-06-09 19:42:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6439754, 955909, 129267, '<td valign="top">Love the warm feeling that this light is giving off. <br/> <br/>not sure I like the frontmost yellow flower, it really wants to pull my eye away from the honey server.</td>', 'Love the warm feeling that this light is giving off.  not sure I like the frontmost yellow flower, it really wants to pull my eye away from the honey server.', '2011-06-09 19:44:20.000000', NULL, 1),
